## Why This Is Asked
Tests experience building production ML pipelines in AWS with strict data locality, latency targets, and privacy. Assesses ability to combine PrivateLink, Lake Formation, Feature Store, canary deployment, drift monitoring, and cost governance.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker PrivateLink
- Lake Formation data access
- Feature Store
- Endpoint traffic splitting (canary)
- Drift detection & retraining triggers
- DP privacy controls and encryption

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example drift score calculation (KS statistic placeholder)
function ksDrift(p, q) {
  let max = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < p.length; i++) {
    max = Math.max(max, Math.abs(p[i] - q[i]));
  }
  return max;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you rollback if canary drift triggers fire?
- What metrics and thresholds would you alert on for latency, FP rate, and drift?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design secure, scalable multi-tenant inference with cross-account PrivateLink, model registry usage, and drift-aware rollouts under cost constraints.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker Model Registry and Pipelines
- PrivateLink across AWS accounts
- Multi-tenant isolation strategies (shared vs. per-tenant containers)
- Drift detection with SageMaker Clarify
- Canary rollout and rollback strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
function routeTenant(input, modelRegistry) {
  const tenant = input.tenantId;
  if (!allowedTenants.has(tenant)) {
    throw new Error('Unauthorized tenant');
  }
  const modelVersion = modelRegistry.getModelVersion(tenant, 'latest');
  return invokeSageMaker(modelVersion.endpoint, input);
}
```
